      "message": "Unconditional 15-second Sleep after rejected PATCH\n\nLocation: Line 94 in lib/bmc_ldap_utils.robot (pre-existing, surfaced by this change)\n\nSuggestion:\n```\n    IF  ${valid_status_codes} \u003d\u003d [${HTTP_OK},${HTTP_NO_CONTENT}]\n        Sleep  15s\n    END\n```\n\nThe sleep exists to allow the LDAP daemon time to restart after a successful configuration update. When a caller expects an error response (HTTP_BAD_REQUEST), the BMC rejects the PATCH without applying any change, so no daemon restart occurs and the 15-second sleep is pure overhead. The condition shown is illustrative; a boolean apply_sleep flag would also work.",
